=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T15:55:33-07:00","id":1447735,"title":"","content":"Really liked this issue.<br /> <br /> A couple of things I found interesting. <br /> <br /> Stating that the twin cities had over 200 vampires. Quick wikipedia search shows 4million in the metro area so about 40 vampires based on the 100,000 estimate vs 200 is a large difference. I've always found that to be rather conservative so 200 doesnt sound very unreasonable for a major metro area. Just interesting how the comics diverge from established knowledge.<br /> <br /> Second am I wrong or did a Justicar diablerize a Kindred in the middle of Elysium? It looked fucking cool but just curious. Also Ian willingly becoming partially blood bound to Cesily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T18:17:14-07:00","id":1447741,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414345-vampire-the-masquerade-winter-s-teeth-discussion-thread?p=1447735#post1447735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really liked this issue.<br /> <br /> A couple of things I found interesting.<br /> <br /> Stating that the twin cities had over 200 vampires. Quick wikipedia search shows 4million in the metro area so about 40 vampires based on the 100,000 estimate vs 200 is a large difference. I've always found that to be rather conservative so 200 doesnt sound very unreasonable for a major metro area. Just interesting how the comics diverge from established knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the comic uses a number that is basically the minimum required to have gangs and wars and in which vampires are men of action, official ratio be damned.<br /> <br /> The official ratio kind of assumes almost everything will be settled politically, with ghouls doing most of what little fighting actually occurs. Which makes more sense in a story about immortals who actually live for centuries, and don't have the death-rate of gang-bangers and goodfelllas. But which makes for a rather boring comicbook.<br /> <br /> Not much of a comic if someone tried to snuff Cecily by having her haven bulldozed in the middle of the day, and her ghouls called their contacts in the unions and tried to have that bulldozing cancelled. And then come sunset, she either heard about how she had been successful in accumulating sufficient worker union influence over the years, or she woke up buried in concrete and slowly starved into torpor. That kind of slow accumulation of political power by a tiny number of widely spread out vampires is what the official canon moves of the Jyhad are about, but, well, canon is really boring. Bureaucrat the Accounting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414345-vampire-the-masquerade-winter-s-teeth-discussion-thread?p=1447735#post1447735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second am I wrong or did a Justicar diablerize a Kindred in the middle of Elysium? It looked fucking cool but just curious. Also Ian willingly becoming partially blood bound to Cesily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I noticed that the way they do blood magic in general is very different from the comics. It seems like in the comic, blood magic is basically blood Obtenebration. Vampires use it for quasi-telekinesis for the most part. There is no suggestion that hunger mechanics exist, since they use it with a casualness that the hunger mechanic precludes. Presumably vampires in the comicverse become hungrier at more or less the same rate as humans, with routine discipline not really speeding this up, at least not more than routine excersize does for a human.<br /> <br /> It's also unclear if blood-bonding exists in this universe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-06-2021, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T19:11:43-07:00","id":1447751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414345-vampire-the-masquerade-winter-s-teeth-discussion-thread?p=1447735#post1447735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really liked this issue.<br /> <br /> A couple of things I found interesting.<br /> <br /> Stating that the twin cities had over 200 vampires. Quick wikipedia search shows 4million in the metro area so about 40 vampires based on the 100,000 estimate vs 200 is a large difference. I've always found that to be rather conservative so 200 doesnt sound very unreasonable for a major metro area. Just interesting how the comics diverge from established knowledge.<br /> <br /> Second am I wrong or did a Justicar diablerize a Kindred in the middle of Elysium? It looked fucking cool but just curious. Also Ian willingly becoming partially blood bound to Cesily.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. To be fair, the 100K to 1 vampire thing was noted IN-UNIVERSE as being the IDEAL ratio of vampire to mortals to keep the Masquerade. Even when it was first proposed, it stated that the World of Darkness was grossly overpopulated vampirewise and that was one of the major reasons there were so many fights going on between the sects.<br /> <br /> 2. I believe the dead Primogen member's husband was a mortal not a vampire. Which actually makes his yelling at Calder Wendt both more impressive as well as stupid. Ian Carfax was kind of REQUIRED to kill a mortal who got that uppity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414345-vampire-the-masquerade-winter-s-teeth-discussion-thread?p=1447741#post1447741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I noticed that the way they do blood magic in general is very different from the comics. It seems like in the comic, blood magic is basically blood Obtenebration. Vampires use it for quasi-telekinesis for the most part. There is no suggestion that hunger mechanics exist, since they use it with a casualness that the hunger mechanic precludes. Presumably vampires in the comicverse become hungrier at more or less the same rate as humans, with routine discipline not really speeding this up, at least not more than routine excersize does for a human.<br /> <br /> It's also unclear if blood-bonding exists in this universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>They gave official stats for the Power that Calder is always using to make little blood puppets. Apparently, it doesn't require a Rouse check. This was more a &quot;Justicar smites a mortal for impudence&quot; sort of moment.<br /> <br /> Note that at his Generation and Blood Potency, Ian Carfax isn't going to need Rouse checks for Discipline uses of 1-3 probably. One of the benefits of being Old and Low Generation is that you don't make Rouse checks nearly as often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-06-2021, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T21:06:01-07:00","id":1447761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414345-vampire-the-masquerade-winter-s-teeth-discussion-thread?p=1447751#post1447751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. I believe the dead Primogen member's husband was a mortal not a vampire. Which actually makes his yelling at Calder Wendt both more impressive as well as stupid. Ian Carfax was kind of REQUIRED to kill a mortal who got that uppity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah if that is the case then really idiotic. <br /> <br /> I think Ali's background is pretty contrived but I can go with it I suppose.<br /> <br /> Cecily seemed to go down pretty easily for a rather strong Ancillae. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T21:20:52-07:00","id":1447762,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to think that Ali isn't long for this comic now. She's now going to be a full-on villain.<br /> <br /> I actually like that Cecily is like, &quot;Ya know, maybe you should kill all vampires in this city!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T22:14:35-07:00","id":1447765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414345-vampire-the-masquerade-winter-s-teeth-discussion-thread?p=1447751#post1447751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They gave official stats for the Power that Calder is always using to make little blood puppets. Apparently, it doesn't require a Rouse check. This was more a &quot;Justicar smites a mortal for impudence&quot; sort of moment.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the telekinesis/obtenebration way they use it is beyond the scope of that first level power description. It's pretty clear that the writer made up his own version of blood magic and the game guys came in afterwards and tried to justify it, and couldn't really do it. Not to mention characters using Potence, Celerity, and Protean more casually than the hunger mechanics really encourage. I stand by my original observation: in the comicbook universe, vampires can just...do things...in the routine casual manner of standard movie/novel vampires. The comicverse is inspired by the game, but doesn't really hold to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1414345-vampire-the-masquerade-winter-s-teeth-discussion-thread?p=1447761#post1447761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cecily seemed to go down pretty easily for a rather strong Ancillae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the one way the vampires seem weaker is that Fortitude isn't really as useful as game Fortitude. On the other hand, sunlight isn't nearly as big a deal in the comicverse as it is in the game. All that indirect sunlight would have fried a game vampire, whereas comic Cecily just watches two vampires fry from a spot that is out of direct sunlight and she's fine.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T00:26:40-07:00","id":1447778,"title":"","content":"1. Eh, I don't think that's the case because they don't seem to do abilities more than would be justified by 5th Edition but I've always felt the idea that vampires are unable to use their powers much vs. previous editions were overstated.<br /> <br /> 2. That was a strange scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.co